@format 1
@id functionality.media-loading.common.list-removal
@title Media loading — common docket removal
@section Functionality
@area Media loading — Common
@entry removal-request
@summary Trace the shared docket-removal consequence used by Files clearing, workspace clearing, relay cleanup, and batch eviction.
@related functionality.media-loading.common.list-selection, functionality.media-loading.global, functionality.media-loading.worklist, functionality.media-loading.funnel
@tag media
@tag loading
@tag common
@tag removal

@alias docket = Cadroue.Application.LDocket
@alias list = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PList

[removal-request] Docket removal request <input>
= A caller has resolved one or more candidate media paths and submits them to the shared docket-removal operation.
> docket-removal

[docket-removal] Docket path removal <decision>
- Remove matching docket entries and publish LDocketRemoved only when at least one existing path is removed @ docket.LDocketPathsRemove(...)
? "At least one path removed" > removal-subscriber
? "No matching path removed" > no-removal

[removal-subscriber] Files removal subscriber <process>
- Rebuild Files state through the docket notification; when the previous current path no longer exists, select the first remaining docket path and publish the clear-change event @ list.PListDocketRemoveHandle(...)
> removal-result

[removal-result] Shared removal consequence <output>
= A remaining media path can become current and reach the scenario-specific selected-path adapter; an empty docket produces no replacement media path.

[no-removal] Removal changes nothing <output>
= No Files selection or viewer request changes because no docket path was removed.
